# Component patterns

- Functional components + hooks. Keep PCF lifecycle in `index.ts`; keep UI in `ContractsGrid/components`.
- `index.ts` `updateView` must return `React.createElement(...)`. Pass `webAPI`, `entityId`, `entityTypeName`, `createContractPageName`, `tokenTheme`.
- Data access only in services (`LeahConfigService`, `LeahAuthService`, `ContractService`). Components do not call `fetch` or `webAPI`.
- New Contract opens custom page `cr964_createcontractpagepoc_cd646` via `openCreateContractSidePanel` (side pane / navigateTo slider). Do not use `alert()`.
- Load with `useCallback` / `useEffect`. Surface failures with Fluent `MessageBar`.
- Do not use `alert()` for product flows—use Fluent `Dialog` or D365 navigation when wiring real actions.
- `generated/ManifestTypes.d.ts` is generated; edit `ControlManifest.Input.xml` then `npm run refreshTypes`.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — service boundary
const data = await ContractService.fetchContractsByEntity(webAPI, entityId, entityTypeName);

// ❌ BAD — fetch inside a component
const res = await fetch(url);
```
